# The Boeing 787-8's control surfaces (src/gfx/parts.hpp says how a line is
# read): each a hinge line from its inboard or lower end to its other, in the
# model's body frame, metres from its origin - +x forward, +y starboard, +z
# down - then how far forward of the hinge the part reaches, how far aft, and
# how far either side of the hinge's plane; and first the JSBSim property
# whose value, in radians, is its deflection, with which way a positive value
# moves its trailing edge.
#
# Measured off the model's own sections (assets/models/787-8.mesh), by
# slicing it where each surface ends: the ailerons between 72% and 92% of the
# wing's semispan, each hinge a quarter of the local chord forward of the
# trailing edge;
# the elevators from 1.6 m out to 8.6 m, hinged three tenths of the
# chord forward of the trailing edge;
# the rudder from 4.0 m above the origin to 11.0 m,
# hinged three tenths of the chord forward of the trailing edge.
# The sections each was measured from are above its lines.
#
# wing -9.23..-5.68 at 21.46 m, -11.91..-9.82 at 27.42 m
surface left-aileron    fcs/left-aileron-pos-rad   down  -8.343 -21.463 -2.614  -11.387 -27.425 -3.447  0.000 1.042 0.386
surface right-aileron   fcs/right-aileron-pos-rad  up    -8.343 21.463 -2.614  -11.387 27.425 -3.447  0.000 1.042 0.386
# tail -27.78..-22.52 at 1.60 m, -30.28..-28.18 at 8.60 m
surface left-elevator   fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -26.202 -1.600 -2.022  -29.649 -8.600 -2.976  0.000 1.834 0.452
surface right-elevator  fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -26.202 1.600 -2.022  -29.649 8.600 -2.976  0.000 1.834 0.452
# fin -26.39..-20.21 at -4.00 m, -29.05..-26.35 at -11.00 m
surface rudder          fcs/rudder-pos-rad         right -24.533 0.001 -4.000  -28.241 -0.002 -11.000  0.000 2.151 0.736
